[
  {
    "sha": "040c114d80414c3d8aa7a2dcbf7c24630099bd6a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDA0MGMxMTRkODA0MTRjM2Q4YWE3YTJkY2JmN2MyNDYzMDA5OWJkNmE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T13:50:40Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T13:50:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse Tormach lathe G76 when the start point is above material\n\nThe LinuxCNC G76 (no entry taper) moves the insert to each pass's cut\ndepth at rapid at the start Z. The Tormach lathe post did not read the\nrecord's StartInAir value (PR #2892), so it posted a G76 that starts\ninside the bar. g76Why now refuses the cycle by name when StartInAir is\nnot true, before any block of the cycle is written. A record without\nthe value (an older cache) is refused until it is regenerated.\n\nThe test support keeps the solid bar (G33 goldens, refusal pins) and\nadds g76_world: the bar ends at its free end face and the cycle starts\none lead out, at Z16, in free air. The goldens follow in a later commit.\n\nRefs #2878\nFixes #2952\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
